    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hi, I’m glad you came in today. What brings you in?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Well, I came in because... I just feel like I got a motor running inside me all day, you know? Like it never shuts off. It's real bad if I have to sit still. Like at church, or sitting out there in the waiting room, or even just at home trying to watch TV. I just feel trapped, like I'm gonna jump out of my skin, and I have to get up and do something. Speaking of church, Pastor Dave was talking about patience this Sunday, and I thought, man, I'd love to have some of that, but my buddy Earl—he sits two pews up—he bought this old Chevy truck he's been fixing up, and I told him he needs to check the carburetor because those things are always acting up, but he wouldn't listen to me. I used to work on cars all the time before... well, anyway, yeah, I just can't sit still. It's driving me crazy.",
