    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Do you ever have times when you feel unusually up or euphoric?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Euphoric? Like... like super happy? Nah, I don't think so. I mean, I get in a good mood sometimes, sure, but not like... not like crazy happy or nothing. Like the other day, I found a twenty dollar bill in the pocket of my old winter coat. I was pretty happy about that. I was just digging in there looking for my keys because I locked myself out of the house again. I do that all the time. Last time I had to pry the screen off the bathroom window, and it bent the frame, so now the bugs get in. We had this huge moth in the living room last night, just flying around the lamp, driving me nuts. I tried to swat it with a rolled-up magazine—it was one of those hunting magazines my cousin gets in the mail. He actually shot a buck last season, ten-pointer. He sent me a picture of it on his phone, but his phone screen is all cracked, so you could barely see the antlers. He dropped it when we were out fishing on the lake. The phone, I mean. But no, I don't get super happy or nothing like that. Just regular, I guess.",
