    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Have you been this fidgety and unable to sit still since you were a kid?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh, yeah. Ever since I was a little kid. Back when I was a boy in school, the teachers were always moving my seat around because I just could not stay put. I was always talking out of turn, and I'd get in big trouble for jumping up before class was even done. Speaking of class being done, they had this really loud bell at my elementary school. Sounded exactly like a fire alarm. Actually, one time, Jimmy Henderson pulled the real fire alarm on a dare. We all had to stand out in the freezing snow for like an hour. Jimmy’s dad owned the hardware store downtown—well, it used to be a hardware store, but now it’s one of those fancy coffee shops where they charge you like six bucks for a tiny little cup. I went in there once and asked for just a regular black coffee, and the guy behind the counter looked at me like I had two heads. He had this weird mustache, you know, the kind you gotta wax so it curls up at the ends? Looked like a cartoon villain or something. I don't know how he drinks anything without getting it all up in his hair. Honestly, I'd just shave it off. It just seems like a lot of work every morning. But... wait, what were you asking me? Something about school?",
