    {
      "turn": 5,
      "doctor_question": "Do you spend a lot of time worrying about things, even when there isn’t a clear reason to worry?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Worrying? I mean, not really. I don't sit around chewing my nails over stuff, if that's what you mean. I got a buddy, Carl, he worries about everything. He's got this old Ford pickup, right? And he's always convinced the transmission is about to drop right out of the bottom of it. I told him, \"Carl, you just gotta check the fluid,\" but he won't listen. He keeps talking about taking it to this mechanic out on Route 9, but that guy is a total rip-off. He charged my brother-in-law four hundred dollars just to look at his brakes. And my brother-in-law, he's not exactly rolling in dough right now because he got laid off from the bottling plant. They shut the whole place down last month. Said something about supply chain issues, but I think the owner just wanted to sell the land to some developers. They're putting up those ugly townhouses everywhere now, the ones with the fake brick on the front and nothing but vinyl siding on the back. They built a whole row of 'em right behind the old bowling alley. Used to love that bowling alley. They had this arcade machine in the corner, Pac-Man, but the joystick always stuck to the left. You had to slam it really hard to get him to turn right. Cost me so many quarters... I used to keep a whole jar of quarters in my room just for that. But nah, I don't really worry about stuff too much. I just kind of go with the flow, you know?",
